# Scratch and toolchain state for the extension lane. Both paths are resolved
# RELATIVE TO THIS DIRECTORY by things that create them, which is why the rules
# live here rather than in the repository root's .gitignore.

# PGRX_HOME. `.cargo/config.toml` forces it to `.pgrx` relative to this directory,
# deliberately: a build must not depend on whatever happens to be in `~/.pgrx` on
# someone's machine. It holds an initialised PostgreSQL install per major and is
# hundreds of megabytes. NO TRAILING SLASH: `cargo pgrx init` ignores the forced
# [env] path and writes to ~/.pgrx, so `just pgrx-init` leaves a SYMLINK here -- and a
# trailing slash matches only real directories, leaving the link untracked-but-offered.
.pgrx

# The suites' scratch root. Extracted extension triplets, battery output and its
# PG15 reference, the regress and cluster and concurrency work directories, the
# parallel suite logs, and every per-run tree under `runs/` when KMONEY_RUN_ROOT
# is set. None of it is source; all of it is regenerated by the run that reads it.
#
# NOTHING IGNORED THIS BEFORE. The repository this came from did not track these
# files but did not ignore them either, so the first YugabyteDB run in a fresh
# checkout would have offered a few hundred logs to `git add -A`.
kamu-money-pg/yb/out/
